
Once upon a time in Stranglethorn Vale, a Gnome Warlock named Gnomer was questing with his Succubus pet, Sirena. They ventured through the treacherous swamps, dodging the aggressive crocolisks and the cunning bandits. Gnomer was impressed with Sirena's stealth and her ability to charm enemies, making their journey smoother. Yet, he often saw other Warlocks with Voidwalkers, who seemed to glide effortlessly through the terrain. One day, as they rested by a river, Gnomer asked Sirena why she wasn't as popular as the Voidwalkers. Sirena replied, "It's because I can't voidwalk, but I can whisper secrets to you, Gnomer, and that's what makes us special."

Answer: The skill of the Succubus that makes them more common than perceived is their ability to whisper secrets, which provides a unique bond with their Warlock owners, despite not having the voidwalk ability. [end of text]


